{"code":"47-2211.00","title":"Sheet Metal Workers","description":"Fabricate, assemble, install, and repair sheet metal products and equipment, such as ducts, control boxes, drainpipes, and furnace casings. Work may involve any of the following: setting up and operating fabricating machines to cut, bend, and straighten sheet metal; shaping metal over anvils, blocks, or forms using hammer; operating soldering and welding equipment to join sheet metal parts; or inspecting, assembling, and smoothing seams and joints of burred surfaces. Includes sheet metal duct installers who install prefabricated sheet metal ducts used for heating, air conditioning, or other purposes.","jobZone":2,"kinds":{"R":{"score":7,"share":0.5882},"I":{"score":2.07,"share":0.1049},"A":{"score":1.55,"share":0.0539},"S":{"score":1,"share":0},"E":{"score":1,"share":0},"C":{"score":3.58,"share":0.2529}},"highPoints":["R","C"],"tasks":[{"id":20642,"text":"Inspect individual parts, assemblies, or installations, using measuring instruments, such as calipers, scales, or micrometers.","core":false,"importance":4.4,"relevance":null,"frequency":null},{"id":5177,"text":"Maintain equipment, making repairs or modifications when necessary.","core":true,"importance":4.3,"relevance":92.87,"frequency":null},{"id":19858,"text":"Fabricate ducts for high efficiency heating, ventilating, and air conditioning (HVAC) systems to maximize efficiency of systems.","core":true,"importance":4.21,"relevance":86.45,"frequency":null},{"id":5173,"text":"Fasten seams or joints together with welds, bolts, cement, rivets, solder, caulks, metal drive clips, or bonds to assemble components into products or to repair sheet metal items.","core":true,"importance":4.17,"relevance":93.55,"frequency":null},{"id":5179,"text":"Transport prefabricated parts to construction sites for assembly and installation.","core":true,"importance":4.17,"relevance":86.15,"frequency":null},{"id":5170,"text":"Install assemblies, such as flashing, pipes, tubes, heating and air conditioning ducts, furnace casings, rain gutters, or downspouts in supportive frameworks.","core":true,"importance":4.15,"relevance":86.74,"frequency":null},{"id":18782,"text":"Hire, train, or supervise new employees or apprentices.","core":true,"importance":4.04,"relevance":91.64,"frequency":null},{"id":20639,"text":"Lay out, measure, and mark dimensions and reference lines on material, such as roofing panels, using calculators, scribes, dividers, squares, or rulers.","core":true,"importance":4,"relevance":90.78,"frequency":null},{"id":5174,"text":"Fabricate or alter parts at construction sites, using shears, hammers, punches, or drills.","core":true,"importance":3.87,"relevance":90.84,"frequency":null},{"id":20638,"text":"Determine project requirements, such as scope, assembly sequences, or required methods or materials, using blueprints, drawings, or written or verbal instructions.","core":true,"importance":3.87,"relevance":96.65,"frequency":null},{"id":20641,"text":"Maneuver completed roofing units into position for installation.","core":true,"importance":3.87,"relevance":84.04,"frequency":2.05},{"id":5169,"text":"Convert blueprints into shop drawings to be followed in the construction or assembly of sheet metal products.","core":false,"importance":3.74,"relevance":60.71,"frequency":null},{"id":5171,"text":"Select gauges or types of sheet metal or nonmetallic material, according to product specifications.","core":true,"importance":3.7,"relevance":98.72,"frequency":null},{"id":5178,"text":"Shape metal material over anvils, blocks, or other forms, using hand tools.","core":true,"importance":3.63,"relevance":75.49,"frequency":null},{"id":19862,"text":"Verify that heating, ventilating, and air conditioning (HVAC) systems are designed, installed, and calibrated in accordance with green certification standards, such as those of Leadership in Energy and Environmental Design (LEED).","core":false,"importance":3.6,"relevance":65.15,"frequency":null},{"